drm/amdkfd: fall back to the dummy cache info on GC 12.1

GC 12.1 takes its cache sizes from the GC info table of IP discovery. A table
of version 2.0 has none, as rocjitsu's ip_discovery.bin does, so KFD reports no
caches and a ROCr built with asserts aborts with "GPU cache info missing".
Use dummy_cache_info then, as every IP version without a table does.

The proper fix is rocjitsu emitting GC info v2.1; this carries the guest until
it does.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_crat.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_crat.c
@@ -1738,6 +1738,10 @@
 				kfd_fill_gpu_cache_info_from_gfx_config(kdev->kfd,
 									cache_line_size_missing,
 									*pcache_info);
+			if (!num_of_cache_types) {
+				*pcache_info = dummy_cache_info;
+				num_of_cache_types = ARRAY_SIZE(dummy_cache_info);
+			}
 			break;
 		default:
 			*pcache_info = dummy_cache_info;
